## Describe the bug

`SchemaComparator.diffTrigger()` skips the expression-vs-introspected-metadata comparison only when the `to` side carries `expression`. Down migrations are generated by diffing in the reverse direction, so from/to swap: `to` is now the introspected side (structured fields + `body`, never `expression`), the guard doesn't hit, and the compare falls through to `diffExpression(from.body, to.body)` with `from.body === undefined` — always "changed".

Effect: every migration generated while an `expression`-form `@Trigger` exists gets a drop+recreate of that trigger in `down()`, even when `up()` never touches it. The recreated DDL is built from introspected metadata and isn't equivalent:

- `createTrigger()` wraps the introspected function body in `begin … end;` again; a body starting with `declare` doesn't match the strip regex in `getAllTriggers()`, so the function comes back double-wrapped (`… as $$ begin declare … begin … end; end; $$`).
- Column scoping is lost: a trigger declared `before insert or update of "alias"` comes back as plain `BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE`.

Still reproduces on 7.1.13 and current master.

## Suggested fix

Skip the comparison when *either* side uses `expression` — same reasoning as the existing comment, just applied symmetrically:

```diff
--- a/packages/sql/src/schema/SchemaComparator.ts
+++ b/packages/sql/src/schema/SchemaComparator.ts
   private diffTrigger(from: SqlTriggerDef, to: SqlTriggerDef): boolean {
     // Raw DDL expression cannot be meaningfully compared to introspected
-    // trigger metadata, so skip diffing when the metadata side uses it.
-    if (to.expression) {
+    // trigger metadata, so skip diffing when only one side uses it.
+    if (to.expression || from.expression) {
       // Both sides have expression — compare the raw DDL directly
-      if (from.expression) {
+      if (from.expression && to.expression) {
         return this.diffExpression(from.expression, to.expression);
       }

-      // Only metadata side has expression — the raw DDL cannot be compared to
+      // Only one side has expression — the raw DDL cannot be compared to
       // introspected metadata. Changes to the expression value won't be detected;
       // drop and recreate the trigger manually to apply expression changes.
       return false;
     }
```

That's what I'm running as a patch locally; generated migrations come out with clean `down()` again.

