### Describe the bug

Recently updated from MikroORM v6 to v7, and have noticed a slight discrepancy in the `EntityRepository.upsert(...)` behaviour, where previously it would not trigger a `NOT NULL constraint` when creating a new entity, and would correctly use the defaults provided.

_Side note:_ Thank you for removing Knex, it was causing **so many** problems being packaged into AWS Lambda, and now it's absolutely bliss.

### Reproduction

Repository: https://github.com/reecebenson/mikro-orm-v7-upsert/
Action: https://github.com/reecebenson/mikro-orm-v7-upsert/actions/runs/23563062505/job/68607675369

I'm using the PostgreSQL driver, however is replicable with the SqliteDriver.

```ts
import { defineEntity, p } from "@mikro-orm/core";
import { v4 } from "uuid";

const UserSchema = defineEntity({
  name: "User",
  properties: {
    id: p
      .string()
      .primary()
      .index()
      .onCreate(() => v4()),
    createdAt: p.datetime().onCreate(() => new Date()),
    updatedAt: p
      .datetime()
      .onCreate(() => new Date())
      .onUpdate(() => new Date()),
    email: p.string().unique().index(),
    name: p.string(),
  },
});

class User extends UserSchema.class {
  name: string = "";
}
UserSchema.setClass(User);

const orm = await MikroORM.init({
  dbName: ":memory:",
  entities: [User],
  debug: ["query", "query-params"],
  allowGlobalContext: true, // only for testing
});
await orm.schema.refresh();

const createUser = new User();
createUser.email = "foo";
createUser.name = "test";

await orm.em.getRepository(User).upsert(createUser); // NotNullConstraintViolationException: NOT NULL constraint failed: user.id
await orm.em.flush();
orm.em.clear();
```

Log from AWS Lambda execution, where I believe instead of the User's `id`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt` using the `onCreate()` and `onUpdate()` hooks, it defaults to `null`, causing the upsert to fail:

```
ERROR	NotNullConstraintViolationException: null value in column "id" of relation "user" violates not-null constraint
 - detail: Failing row contains (null, null, null, foo, test)
```

